# AGX Thor, LLM sharing the board's single GPU with RT-CV, RT-Embed and
# streamprocessing. The VLM is remote in this configuration: dev-profile.sh
# rejects a local LLM alongside a local VLM on this board, because the two do not
# fit together (measured 2026-08-31 -- see the both-local check in process_args).
#
# Thor's 128 GB is *unified* memory shared with the host, not dedicated VRAM, and
# CUDA reports 122.82 GiB of it. vLLM requires
#   free_memory >= NIM_GPU_MEM_FRACTION x total_memory
# at init_device(), before weights load, and does not subtract memory held by
# other processes. So this is a floor on what must be FREE at startup, not a
# ceiling on what gets used -- if something else got there first, the engine
# refuses to start rather than shrinking to fit.
#
# 0.30 asks for 36.85 GiB. The INT4 profile needs 32 GiB, so there is only ~5 GiB
# of slack: lowering this much below 0.27 trades a startup failure for a model
# that cannot load at all.
#
# Verified failing at 0.30 when a local RT-VLM was also resident:
#   "Free memory on device cuda:0 (29.29/122.82 GiB) on startup is less than
#    desired GPU memory utilization (0.3, 36.85 GiB)"
# which is the case the both-local rejection now prevents.
NIM_KVCACHE_PERCENT=0.30
NIM_GPU_MEM_FRACTION=0.30
# Matches the GB300 search value. The checkpoint declares far more, but KV pages
# scale with context x concurrency and this board has neither the pool nor the
# bandwidth for it.
NIM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=32000
MAX_JOBS=4
# Parse reasoning separately and support OpenAI-compatible automatic tool calls.
# --max-num-seqs 2 matches GB300 search: search issues few concurrent LLM calls,
# and each additional slot costs KV pages this board cannot spare.
NIM_PASSTHROUGH_ARGS="--reasoning-parser nemotron_v3 --enable-auto-tool-choice --tool-call-parser qwen3_coder --max-num-seqs 2"
# INT4 (vllm-int4-tp1-pp1-32.0) is the arch-neutral tp1 profile: it is the only
# one whose arm64 manifest entry carries no GPU allow-list, just a 32 GB floor.
# Re-derive with `list-model-profiles` if the image tag changes.
NIM_MODEL_PROFILE=2ef85c7286907e706eb0d6c4750a1aefa719447097d151ab34c7837fc02bdac4
